{"obs_mudm1dck_0dff6f8ea014":{"hookType":"prompt_submit","id":"obs_mudm1dck_0dff6f8ea014","origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-23T04:35:55.955Z","channel":"user"},"raw":{"prompt":"A previous agent produced the plan below to accomplish the user's task. Implement the plan in a fresh context. Treat the plan as the source of user intent, re-read files as needed, and carry the work through implementation and verification.\n\n# Fix KiCanvas loading in development\n\n## Summary\n\nThe reported Vite error comes from [pcbViewer.ts](/home/chris/01_Projects/ts-boardstudio2/app/src/utils/pcbViewer.ts): it dynamically imports `kicanvas.js` from `public`. Vite serves [public assets by URL](https://github.com/vitejs/vite/blob/v5.4.21/docs/guide/assets.md), without processing them as source imports. The error points to PCB preview startup; the generated board and download follow a separate path.\n\n## Changes\n\n- First add a regression for loading the viewer from its public URL and confirm it fails with the current loader.\n- Replace the dynamic import with an on-demand script element. Keep the revisioned URL, one shared pending load, custom-element initialization check, and retry after a load failure.\n- Leave PCB generation, the KiCanvas bundle, and unrelated worktree edits untouched. No public API changes are needed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Confirm the regression passes after the change, including concurrent loads and failure followed by retry.\n- Open PCB preview through the Vite development server: no `/dependencies/kicanvas.js` server error, and the board renders.\n- Check the built preview and first offline load. Confirm the generated `.kicad_pcb` remains downloadable. If headless Chromium lacks WebGL2, use SwiftShader for the rendering check.\n\n## Assumption\n\nThe Vite error is the reported breakage. If generation still fails after the viewer loads, diagnose that as a separate failure using the generated output and browser error.\n"},"sessionId":"01a0cc8c-7ee9-7362-96e0-740c61cb1eed","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:35:55.955Z","userPrompt":"A previous agent produced the plan below to accomplish the user's task. Implement the plan in a fresh context. Treat the plan as the source of user intent, re-read files as needed, and carry the work through implementation and verification.\n\n# Fix KiCanvas loading in development\n\n## Summary\n\nThe reported Vite error comes from [pcbViewer.ts](/home/chris/01_Projects/ts-boardstudio2/app/src/utils/pcbViewer.ts): it dynamically imports `kicanvas.js` from `public`. Vite serves [public assets by URL](https://github.com/vitejs/vite/blob/v5.4.21/docs/guide/assets.md), without processing them as source imports. The error points to PCB preview startup; the generated board and download follow a separate path.\n\n## Changes\n\n- First add a regression for loading the viewer from its public URL and confirm it fails with the current loader.\n- Replace the dynamic import with an on-demand script element. Keep the revisioned URL, one shared pending load, custom-element initialization check, and retry after a load failure.\n- Leave PCB generation, the KiCanvas bundle, and unrelated worktree edits untouched. No public API changes are needed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Confirm the regression passes after the change, including concurrent loads and failure followed by retry.\n- Open PCB preview through the Vite development server: no `/dependencies/kicanvas.js` server error, and the board renders.\n- Check the built preview and first offline load. Confirm the generated `.kicad_pcb` remains downloadable. If headless Chromium lacks WebGL2, use SwiftShader for the rendering check.\n\n## Assumption\n\nThe Vite error is the reported breakage. If generation still fails after the viewer loads, diagnose that as a separate failure using the generated output and browser error.\n"},"obs_mudm1hjv_cd9462edf186":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mudm1hjv_cd9462edf186","origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-23T04:36:01.399Z","channel":"tool"