ew.tsx`/`PcbPreview.tsx` embed KiCanvas, but the release needs actionable load-error UI and a shared net registry for pads, segments, arcs, vias, zones, inspection, and highlighting. [Task 1]\n881:- BHK is deployed in the GUI as `src/examples/bhk.ts`; custom footprints are staged from `vendor/bhk/footprints/` through `patch/footprints_index.js`/`patch/patch_ergogen.sh`. Commit `3c30c6b` deployed successfully; live Playwright passed gallery load, PCB generation, KiCanvas preview, download, and offline byte-identical regeneration. The gallery control is a label: use `getByLabel('Load BHK example', { exact: true })`, not a button-role selector. [Task 5]\n884:- The workspace root is not a Git repository: inspect child repositories with `git -C ergogen`, `git -C ergogen-gui`, and `git -C bhk`. Ergogen uses npm/Mocha/Rollup, the GUI uses pnpm/Vite/Vitest/Playwright plus `pnpm run precommit`, and BHK has only a placeholder failing `npm test`. [Task 4]\n889:- The checked-in GUI bundle reports Ergogen 4.2.1; never release before a successful candidate rebuild confirms the embedded 5.0.0 version. `gh auth status` was invalid, and Vite’s empty `PUBLIC_URL` does not match `/ergogen-gui/`; validate repository/npm/Pages permissions and production asset, worker, router, and service-worker paths first. [Task 1]\n890:- Do not release the GUI preparation: full GUI build/precommit/Playwright, lockfile refresh, bundled Ergogen rebuild, native KiCanvas named-net support, and actionable preview errors were not completed because GitHub/npm DNS and dependencies were unavailable. [Task 2]\n"},"sessionId":"01a0cc8c-7ee9-7362-96e0-740c61cb1eed","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:36:01.418Z","toolInput":{"command":"rg -n \"KiCanvas|kicanvas|pcbViewer|Vite\" /home/chris/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"},"toolName":"Bash","toolOutput":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1355)\nTotal output lines: 18\n\n232:- For this Node 26 app, run full Vitest/precommit checks with `NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimen