m config.webServer was not able to start. Exit code: 1\n\n\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"},"sessionId":"01a0cc8c-7ee9-7362-96e0-740c61cb1eed","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:38:10.668Z","toolInput":{"command":"NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimental-webstorage pnpm --dir app exec playwright test e2e/app.spec.ts e2e/offline.spec.ts --grep 'creates a matrix draft and previews its PCB|opens the PCB viewer for the first time offline' --reporter=line"},"toolName":"Bash","toolOutput":"(node:14) [DEP0205] DeprecationWarning: `module.register()` is deprecated. Use `module.registerHooks()` instead.\n(Use `node --trace-deprecation ...` to show where the warning was created)\nError: Process from config.webServer was not able to start. Exit code: 1\n\n\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"},"obs_mudm4cnx_a194e065d864":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mudm4cnx_a194e065d864","origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-23T04:38:15.034Z","channel":"tool","detail":"Bash"},"raw":{"tool_input":{"command":"ss -ltnp '( sport = :3000 )'"},"tool_name":"Bash","tool_output":"Cannot open netlink socket: Operation not permitted\nState Recv-Q Send-Q Local Address:Port Peer Address:PortProcess\n"},"sessionId":"01a0cc8c-7ee9-7362-96e0-740c61cb1eed","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:38:15.034Z","toolInput":{"command":"ss -ltnp '( sport = :3000 )'"},"toolName":"Bash","toolOutput":"Cannot open netlink socket: Operation not permitted\nState Recv-Q Send-Q Local Address:Port Peer Address:PortProcess\n"},"obs_mudm4cz5_e008a24e0787":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mudm4cz5_e008a24e0787","origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-23T04:38:15.438Z","channel":"tool","detail":"Bash"},"raw":{"tool_input":{"command":"pnpm --dir app exec vite preview --host 127.0.0.1 --port 3000 --strictPort"},"tool_name":"Bash","tool_output":"error when starting preview server:\nError: listen EPERM: operation not permitted 127.0.0.1:3000\n    at Server.setupListenHandle [as _listen2] (node:net:2306:21)\n    at listenInCluster (node:net:2437:12)\n    at node:net:2666:7\n    at process.processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:90:21)\n"},"sessionId":"01a0cc8c-7ee9-7362-96e0-740c61cb1eed","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:38:15.438Z","toolInput":{"command":"pnpm --dir app exec vite preview --host 127.0.0.1 --port 3000 --strictPort"},"toolName":"Bash","toolOutput":"error when starting preview server:\nError: listen EPERM: operation not permitted 127.0.0.1:3000\n    at Server.setupListenHandle [as _listen2] (node:net:2306:21)\n    at listenInCluster (node:net:2437:12)\n    at node:net:2666:7\n    at process.processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:90:21)\n"},"obs_mudm4nki_6b1b0585b6ba":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mudm4nki_6b1b0585b6ba","origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-23T04:38:29.167Z","channel":"tool","detail":"Bash"},"raw":{"tool_input":{"command":"nl -ba /home/chris/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '595,602p'; nl -ba app/src/utils/pcbViewer.ts | head -70; nl -ba app/src/utils/pcbViewer.test.ts | head -100"},"tool_name":"Bash","tool_output":"   595\t- Do not pre-validate a drag in a worker before committing it; `StudioCanvas` waits for `useLayoutAnalysis(candidate)` and `BoardStudio.move()` refuses edits while stale/pending, causing blocking/snapback. Commit immediately, defer `addOutline()` until the current `LayoutReport`, and invalidate obsolete worker output on edits, undo, imports, and project switches. Do not repair imported designs until an explicit edit or rebuild. [Task 11]\n   596\t- A clean comparison checkout reproduced 287 engine passes plus 18 DXF fixture failures. Report those fixtures as pre-existing, never as a green engine suite. Initial snapping-menu checks were asynchronous; use `expect.poll` for bounding-box assertions. [Task 12]\n   597\t- If precommit reports Markdownlint MD041, restore `# Changelog` as the first top-level heading before rerunning. [Task 12]\n   598\t- Before row/column assertions, convert a `free` arrangement to columns/rows; a scalar thumb pitch yields `must be array`. Do not use `resizeCluster(..., mode: 'fill')` for BHK: it fills intentional holes. [Task 13]\n   599\t- The BHK migrated PCB is not byte-identical: normalized footprint/copper/net content matched, but parametric trigonometry changed outline coordinates by up to ~0.000671 mm. Attribute unscoped precommit/prebuild vendor/library failures only after isolating vendor state. [Task 13]\n   600\t- `PCB preview unavailable: Unable to create WebGL2 context` in Xvfb is an environment rendering limit; rerun Chromium with SwiftShader for KiCanvas/browser CAD checks. [Task 13]\n   601\t- `plate_gap / 2` entered through the stack editor can self-reference and throw `Cyclic parameter: plate_gap`; reject/rewrite self-referential parameter expressions before storing. Material fit for an unlinked case must use local dimensions, topology changes must update overridden assemblies without discarding other customizations, and name-only Setup drafts must not restore stale pitch. A column-guide alignment failure (`Solved layout does not satisfy this driving rule`) needs solver-consistent guide geometry. Passing focused engine tests alone did not expose these five regressions; retain targeted Vitest, Playwright, and direct-engine probes. [Task 14]\n   602\t\n     1\tconst VIEWER_REVISION = 'kicad10-unconnected-pads-1';\n     2\tlet pending: Promise<void> | undefined;\n     3\t\n     4\t// Load on demand, with a revisioned URL so offline caches cannot retain an older parser.\n     5\texport function loadPcbViewer(): Promise<void> {\n     6\t  if (\n     7\t    customElements.get('kicanvas-embed') &&\n     8\t    customElements.get('kicanvas-source')\n     9\t  ) {\n    10\t    return Promise.resolve();\n    11\t  }\n    12\t  if (!pending) {\n    13\t    const url = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}dependencies/kicanvas.js?v=${VIEWER_REVISION}`;\n    14\t    const script = document.createElement('script');\n    15\t    script.src = url;\n    16\t    script.async = true;\n    17\t\n    18\t    // Public bundles load as scripts; confirm registration before showing the viewer.\n    19\t    pending = new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) => {\n    20\t      script.onload = () => {\n    21\t        if (\n    22\t          !customElements.get('kicanvas-embed') ||\n    23\t          !customElements.get('kicanvas-source')\n    24\t        ) {\n    25\t          reject(new Error('KiCanvas did not initialize.'));\n    26\t          return;\n    27\t        }\n    28\t        resolve();\n    29\t      };\n    30\t      script.onerror = () => reject(new Error('KiCanvas failed to load.'));\n    31\t      document.head.appendChild(script);\n    32\t    }).catch((error: unknown) => {\n    33\t      script.remove();\n    34\t      pending = undefined;\n    35\t      throw error;\n    36\t    });\n    37\t  }\n    38\t  return pending;\n    39\t}\n     1\timport { beforeEach, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';\n     2\t\n     3\tbeforeEach(() => {\n     4\t  vi.resetModules();\n     5\t  document.head\n     6\t    .querySelectorAll('script[src*=\"kicanvas.js\"]')\n     7\t    .forEach((script) => {\n     8\t      script.remove();\n     9\t    });\n    10\t});\n    11\t\n    12\tit('loads one public script for concurrent preview requests', async () => {\n    13\t  const elements = vi.spyOn(customElements, 'get').mockReturnValue(undefined);\n    14\t  const { loadPcbViewer } = await import('./pcbViewer');\n    15\t\n    16\t  const first = loadPcbViewer();\n    17\t  const second = loadPcbViewer();\n    18\t  const script = document.head.querySelector<HTMLScriptElement>(\n    19\t    'script[src*=\"dependencies/kicanvas.js\"]'\n    20\t  );\n    21\t\n    22\t  expect(first).toBe(second);\n    23\t  expect(script?.src).toContain(\n    24\t    '/dependencies/kicanvas.js?v=kicad10-unconnected-pads-1'\n    25\t  );\n    26\t  expect(\n    27\t    document.head.querySelectorAll('script[src*=\"kicanvas.js\"]')\n    28\t  ).toHaveLength(1);\n    29\t\n    30\t  elements.mockReturnValue(class extends HTMLElement {});\n    31\t  script?.dispatchEvent(new Event('load'));\n    32\t  await expect(first).resolves.toBeUndefined();\n    33\t  await expect(second).resolves.toBeUndefined();\n    34\t  elements.mockRestore();\n    35\t});\n    36\t\n    37\tit('retries after a script load fails', async () => {\n    38\t  const elements = vi.spyOn(customElements, 'get').mockReturnValue(undefined);\n    39\t  const { loadPcbViewer } = await import('./pcbViewer');\n    40\t\n    41\t  const first = loadPcbViewer();\n    42\t  const failedScript = document.head.querySelector<HTMLScriptElement>(\n    43\t    'script[src*=\"dependencies/kicanvas.js\"]'\n    44\t  );\n    45\t  failedScript?.dispatchEvent(new Event('error'));\n    46\t  await expect(first).rejects.toThrow();\n    47\t\n    48\t  const retry = loadPcbViewer();\n    49\t  const scripts = document.head.querySelectorAll<HTMLScriptElement>(\n    50\t    'script[src*=\"dependencies/kicanvas.js\"]'\n    51\t  );\n    52\t  expect(scripts).toHaveLength(1);\n    53\t  expect(scripts[0]).not.toBe(failedScript);\n    54\t\n    55\t  elements.mockReturnValue(class extends HTMLElement {});\n    56\t  scripts[0].dispatchEvent(new Event('load'));\n    57\t  await expect(retry).resolves.toBeUndefined();\n    58\t  elements.mockRestore();\n    59\t});\n"},"sessionId":"01a0cc8c-7ee9-7362-96e0-740c61cb1eed","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:38:29.167Z","toolInput":{"command":"nl -ba /home/chris/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '595,602p'; nl -ba app/src/utils/pcbViewer.ts | head -70; nl -ba app/src/utils/pcbViewer.test.ts | head -100"},"toolName":"Bash","toolOutput":"   595\t- Do not pre-validate a drag in a worker before committing it; `StudioCanvas` waits for `useLayoutAnalysis(candidate)` and `BoardStudio.move()` refuses edits while stale/pending, causing blocking/snapback. Commit immediately, defer `addOutline()` until the current `LayoutReport`, and invalidate obsolete worker output on edits, undo, imports, and project switches. Do not repair imported designs until an explicit edit or rebuild. [Task 11]\n   596\t- A clean comparison checkout reproduced 287 engine passes plus 18 DXF fixture failures. Report those fixtures as pre-existing, never as a green engine suite. Initial snapping-menu checks were asynchronous; use `expect.poll` for bounding-box assertions. [Task 12]\n   597\t- If precommit reports Markdownlint MD041, restore `# Changelog` as the first top-level heading before rerunning. [Task 12]\n   598\t- Before row/column assertions, convert a `free` arrangement to columns/rows; a scalar thumb pitch yields `must be array`. Do not use `resizeCluster(..., mode: 'fill')` for BHK: it fills intentional holes. [Task 13]\n   599\t- The BHK migrated PCB is not byte-identical: normalized footprint/copper/net content matched, but parametric trigonometry changed outline coordinates by up to ~0.000671 mm. Attribute unscoped precommit/prebuild vendor/library failures only after isolating vendor state. [Task 13]\n   600\t- `PCB preview unavailable: Unable to create WebGL2 context` in Xvfb is an environment rendering limit; rerun Chromium with SwiftShader for KiCanvas/browser CAD checks. [Task 13]\n   601\t- `plate_gap / 2` entered through the stack editor can self-reference and throw `Cyclic parameter: plate_gap`; reject/rewrite self-referential parameter expressions before storing. Material fit for an unlinked case must use local dimensions, topology changes must update overridden assemblies without discarding other customizations, and name-only Setup drafts must not restore stale pitch. A column-guide alignment failure (`Solved layout does not satisfy this driving rule`) needs solver-consistent guide geometry. Passing focused engine tests alone did not expose these five regressions; retain targeted Vitest, Playwright, and direct-engine probes. [Task 14]\n   602\t\n     1\tconst VIEWER_REVISION = 'kicad10-unconnected-pads-1';\n     2\tlet pending: Promise<void> | undefined;\n     3