sk 9]\n- Branch consolidation used `/home/chris/01_Projects/ergogen10/branch-consolidation`; seven original checkout HEADs and 172 backed-up dirty files remained byte-identical. `retire-branches.py` is read-only by default and requires archive-tag verification, exact expected SHAs, and deletion leases. [Task 10]\n- Local Studio candidate validation passed 702 unit tests and 58 active Playwright tests (one existing skip), with direct Studio startup, persistence, PCB/BHK/enclosure flows, SVG import, offline behavior, models/footprints, and exports checked at `http://localhost:4319/ergogen-gui/`. Hidden-input tests should await `page.waitForEvent('filechooser')` before clicking, then call `fileChooser.setFiles(...)`. [Task 10]\n- `addOutline()` is the sole outline builder and requires a current `LayoutReport` for reliable generated bridges. Automatic outlines use `fill` for incidental voids while retaining explicit cutouts/protected gaps; a single `meta.studio.outline.auto` setting defaults to enabled, while disabled mode retains a serialized line/arc snapshot and manual rebuild. [Task 11]\n- `layoutOnly: true` was ~100 ms versus ~564 ms full analysis on the synthetic fixture. The planned coordinator commits on release, then stages layout -> outline -> board analysis after 180 ms coalescing; accept results only when source/injection/library/asset revisions match and amend generated outline updates into the originating history entry. [Task 11]\n- Native layout guides are references, not objects: `src/native/guides.js` computes physical centers/row-column frames; `layoutSnapping.ts` handles grid/center/origin/edge snapping; `layoutRelations.ts` creates and unlinks persistent relationships. `boardDefaults` starts native designs with explicit `u`/`v` pitch and preserves authored spacing/layout object…353 tokens truncated…]\n- Symptom: sketch editing or assembly preview consumes legacy results, a Code/library transition loses the workspace, or a tray preview has no STL. Fix: route through shared analysis/generation, retain a `codeReturn` target with a focused test, and convert within cancellable `useCasePreview`. [Task 1]\n- Do not claim a cloud continuation runs successfully merely because its thread exists; at rollout end the cloud thread had no verified response. Do not merge default, deploy, publish, alter BHK, or claim hardware fit without follow-up authorization. [Task 3]\n- An empty Custom Libraries list does not prove bundled footprints are absent: trace the worker-generated catalogue and the UI rendering path. Tests for a collapsed catalogue must open `<details>` before asserting its entries. [Task 4]\n- Unit tests are not visual proof. For preview/assembly/outline claims, run focused browser states in addition to engine/GUI suites. Physical fit and fabrication readiness remain separate evidence gates. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 5]\n- If `tsc` produces a huge count, identify configuration-layer causes before suppressing errors: adding `vitest/globals` reduced 1,792 errors to 268 and exposed the legacy Jest alias as the dominant cause. [Task 6]\n- The initial architecture review missed the newer `enclosure-work` checkout and overstated missing capabilities. Inspect all active worktrees before proposing a redesign. At Task 7 rollout end the layout-editor changes were uncommitted; inspect the current worktree rather than assuming that state still holds. [Task 7]\n- Do not conflate pre-existing `require('makerjs')` startup and third-party bundle/WASM warnings with layout-editor regressions; reproduce them against the changed path before treating them as new failures. [Task 7]\n- The Task 8 coordinator rollout did not complete a full precommit, production build, or browser pass. Focused tests and subagent reports are not full integration verification; rerun those gates before treating branch-consolidation changes as complete. Keep geometry conversion helpers scoped inside their traversal function: an out-of-scope helper in `studioOutli